  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "If $P=QR$, where \n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 6 & -3\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]$, then ${p}_{34}=$",
  "worked_solution": "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $Q$ by the $4$th column in $R$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}_{34} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 4 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-4-8+8+20 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
